From 1d3eeaf9d6d9487e562a6bd223aa669ea6ee7013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:24:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] helpers/envkernel.sh: build kernels with ccache

Every envkernel compile ran uncached, for three reasons:

- The make alias sets CCACHE_DISABLE=1 on the command itself, so nothing
  outside can override it, and pmbootstrap's --no-ccache/ccache setting
  only reaches package builds.
- ccache was not necessarily installed in the native chroot, where the
  compile runs.
- Alpine's ccache ships masquerade links for gcc, cc, g++ and c++ but none
  for clang, and envkernel builds with clang by default (LLVM=1).

Point CCACHE_DIR at the cache pmbootstrap already mounts in the native
chroot (cache_ccache_$ARCH at /mnt/pmbootstrap/ccache) instead of the
/home/pmos/.ccache symlink, install ccache with the other build
dependencies, and add the clang and clang++ links.

Upstream disabled the cache in 2022 (MR 2189) as a performance judgement,
since envkernel builds are incremental anyway. They are not after a clean,
a branch switch or a re-created native chroot. The porthole workspace has
run with these three changes since 2026-08: touching one widely included
header and rebuilding a kernel took 1m49s uncached, 2m09s with a cold cache
and 43s with a warm one (320 of 321 hits), also after the native chroot was
deleted and re-created.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 helpers/envkernel.sh | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/helpers/envkernel.sh b/helpers/envkernel.sh
index 75bf5da..a86720f 100644
--- a/helpers/envkernel.sh
+++ b/helpers/envkernel.sh
@@ -189,6 +189,7 @@ initialize_chroot() {
 		bc \
 		binutils \
 		bison \
+		ccache \
 		clang-libclang \
 		diffutils \
 		elfutils-dev \
@@ -228,6 +229,10 @@ may not be available on stable releases.\n\n"
 		[ -n "$has_shwordsplit" ] && unset has_shwordsplit
 	fi
 
+	# ccache masquerades as gcc, but Alpine's ccache has no links for clang
+	"$pmbootstrap" -q chroot -- ln -sf ../../../bin/ccache /usr/lib/ccache/bin/clang
+	"$pmbootstrap" -q chroot -- ln -sf ../../../bin/ccache /usr/lib/ccache/bin/clang++
+
 	# Create /mnt/linux
 	sudo mkdir -p "$chroot/mnt/linux"
 
@@ -278,7 +283,8 @@ set_alias_make() {
 	# Build make command
 	cmd="echo '*** pmbootstrap envkernel.sh active for $PWD! ***';"
 	cmd="$cmd pmbootstrap -q chroot --user --"
-	cmd="$cmd CCACHE_DISABLE=1"
+	# ccache: the dir pmbootstrap mounts for it in the native chroot
+	cmd="$cmd CCACHE_DIR=/mnt/pmbootstrap/ccache"
 	cmd="$cmd ARCH=$arch"
 	if [ "$need_cross_compiler" = 1 ]; then
 		cmd="$cmd CROSS_COMPILE=$cross_compiler"
